## Original Content
Monashees, one of Latin America's oldest and most influential VC firms, believes the next phase of the region's startup ecosystem requires a permanent Silicon Valley presence, opening a San Francisco office last year. We spoke with firm partner Fabiola Quinzaños to talk through the firm's evolution and how it is meeting this AI moment.

## Summary
Monashees, a leading Latin American VC firm, has established a permanent Silicon Valley presence by opening a San Francisco office. The firm discusses its evolution and how it is adapting to the AI era to support the region's startup ecosystem.

## Key Points
- Monashees is one of Latin America's oldest and most influential VC firms.
- The firm believes a Silicon Valley presence is essential for the next phase of Latin America's startup ecosystem.
- Monashees opened a San Francisco office last year to solidify its expansion.
- The firm is evolving and focusing on AI trends, as discussed with partner Fabiola Quinzaños.


